 #uuid "10847312-dde2-55cc-bbce-32b3f2b8723c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9fafb82-f857-530c-a571-da4ddd2c07e3" :answer/id #uuid "a9fafb82-f857-530c-a571-da4ddd2c07e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74f96a2a-40d7-5dbb-8c3c-8b0e155b91b2" :answer/id #uuid "74f96a2a-40d7-5dbb-8c3c-8b0e155b91b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e30ad71c-64f9-5534-85f8-dfc05dd3aec9" :answer-field/id #uuid "e30ad71c-64f9-5534-85f8-dfc05dd3aec9" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b8ab8f31-61b0-55ea-ace1-21a1ef7ae4b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ed7b269f-953a-54fa-9e61-dd5a4919e14b" "answer-b234bb98-5a1b-545d-ada5-467b2dd8155c" "answer-3d3b3d04-e35f-505f-8628-7f7927d01651" "answer-b8ab8f31-61b0-55ea-ace1-21a1ef7ae4b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed7b269f-953a-54fa-9e61-dd5a4919e14b" :answer/id #uuid "ed7b269f-953a-54fa-9e61-dd5a4919e14b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b234bb98-5a1b-545d-ada5-467b2dd8155c" :answer/id #uuid "b234bb98-5a1b-545d-ada5-467b2dd8155c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d3b3d04-e35f-505f-8628-7f7927d01651" :answer/id #uuid "3d3b3d04-e35f-505f-8628-7f7927d01651" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8ab8f31-61b0-55ea-ace1-21a1ef7ae4b9" :answer/id #uuid "b8ab8f31-61b0-55ea-ace1-21a1ef7ae4b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a28a184f-09e4-5b7a-afed-9fba64c7681f" :answer-field/id #uuid "a28a184f-09e4-5b7a-afed-9fba64c7681f" :answer-field/key "field-9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-a985dc98-856f-5899-b505-9bb6d7181bbd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a985dc98-856f-5899-b505-9bb6d7181bbd" "answer-a906b6a2-e624-5b7a-9c6a-5d61f4dd8b46" "answer-edfc2d51-e6ed-52ec-aeff-d609a8e46c06" "answer-d7e4725a-6905-5048-8a8c-18f3d175b967"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a985dc98-856f-5899-b505-9bb6d7181bbd" :answer/id #uuid "a985dc98-856f-5899-b505-9bb6d7181bbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a906b6a2-e624-5b7a-9c6a-5d61f4dd8b46" :answer/id #uuid "a906b6a2-e624-5b7a-9c6a-5d61f4dd8b46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-edfc2d51-e6ed-52ec-aeff-d609a8e46c06" :answer/id #uuid "edfc2d51-e6ed-52ec-aeff-d609a8e46c06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7e4725a-6905-5048-8a8c-18f3d175b967" :answer/id #uuid "d7e4725a-6905-5048-8a8c-18f3d175b967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162045 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0ba1751d-87a5-51c1-9c47-8e0f1eb46649"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0ba1751d-87a5-51c1-9c47-8e0f1eb46649" :question/id #uuid "0ba1751d-87a5-51c1-9c47-8e0f1eb46649" :question/math-academy-id "q-363846" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$  select the correct options in the computations of the matrix $U$ below.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce the singular values ${\\sigma }_{1}=2\\sqrt{3}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\n\nNow, we compute the $1$st column of $U.$ It is given by:\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${u}_{1}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  |  | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}$ |  |  |\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal.\n\nHence, we must find vectors $u=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}]^{T}$ such that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nChoosing ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ as free variables, the general solution is given by:\n\n|  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | ${x}_{2}$ |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} |  |  |\n\nthat we can rewrite as:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nNext, we orthogonalize ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ using the Gram-Schmidt process to get the corresponding orthogonal vectors ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nLet ${c}_{1}={b}_{1},$ then:\n\n|  |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${c}_{2}=\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-7}} |  |  |\n\nFinally, normalizing orthogonal vectors ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ we obtain the second and third columns of $U:$   \n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\">\n                ${u}_{2}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"90px\">\n                {{field-8}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-9}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                $-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\">\n                ${u}_{3}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"90px\">\n                {{field-10}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-11}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=2\\sqrt{3}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\nAlso, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$\n\nTherefore, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find vectors \n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0$ and $‖u‖=1.$\n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}{x}_{2}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get the general solution \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are free variables. \n\nNotice that the two linearly independent solutions ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ are *not* mutually orthogonal. Therefore, we have to orthogonalize them using the Gram-Schmidt process. So, let \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}={b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} & ={b}_{2}-\\frac{{b}_{2}\\cdot {c}_{1}}{{c}_{1}\\cdot {c}_{1}}{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{2}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, normalizing orthogonal vectors ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ we obtain the second and third columns of $U:$   \n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],\\,{u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix $U$ could be the following:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6da967d6-d976-50e9-b6e8-2bf048a89c09" "answer-field-0faa78a6-bc0d-5b1a-81d5-d7da44eef726" "answer-field-b170cc6e-aab5-529c-9896-73a300941daf" "answer-field-fc6db4d2-ea1d-5421-a0db-e24e2e0720aa" "answer-field-d4931c23-68ae-5da4-81ee-3c97dd4f6730" "answer-field-dc8e70a8-daaa-5f24-ad61-245827641b0b" "answer-field-608c74ef-2e40-50bb-a3dd-612f0b7f32be" "answer-field-03b01ee8-41bf-5748-a07b-1c8fbdd71f8c" "answer-field-a13e3d99-fba3-50fa-9a5a-4b01be61fc45" "answer-field-d9812805-4969-5cfb-a3b4-aa190fc21fbd" "answer-field-c3e24bc6-ac06-5a06-8592-1925604d6477"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6da967d6-d976-50e9-b6e8-2bf048a89c09" :answer-field/id #uuid "6da967d6-d976-50e9-b6e8-2bf048a89c09" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-15dcf2d0-a1ce-5d9f-971d-640aac12ecec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d837dc93-0d93-52c2-8cbb-fbb734eabf04" "answer-fbbd2217-15f7-54a9-bf0a-dedd25a122f8" "answer-15dcf2d0-a1ce-5d9f-971d-640aac12ecec" "answer-4948e427-32da-5a11-bfbd-df8004aec6d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d837dc93-0d93-52c2-8cbb-fbb734eabf04" :answer/id #uuid "d837dc93-0d93-52c2-8cbb-fbb734eabf04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbbd2217-15f7-54a9-bf0a-dedd25a122f8" :answer/id #uuid "fbbd2217-15f7-54a9-bf0a-dedd25a122f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15dcf2d0-a1ce-5d9f-971d-64